  "title": "Vendor Stacks Are Dead. Long Live the DealershipOS.",
  "summary": "Almost every product on a dealer’s software stack was designed for a system-of-record dealer and a Saturday walk-in buyer. Neither exists anymore. The vendor stack is the obituary; the DealershipOS, a single operating layer holding the ledger, the conversation surface, the transaction engine, and the storefront, is the replacement.",
